---
/**
 * Privacy notice.
 *
 * Written to match what this site actually does, not from a generator: the
 * only personal data collected is what someone types into /contact/ or
 * /start/, which the Worker hands to Resend and drops into an inbox.
 *
 * If the stack changes (analytics added, a CRM introduced, the Worker starts
 * storing submissions in KV or D1) this page has to change with it, or it
 * stops being true. It is a plain-language description of the processing, not
 * legal advice: worth a read-through by someone qualified before you lean on
 * it commercially.
 */
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Schema from "../../components/Schema.astro";
import { webPageSchema, breadcrumbSchema } from "../../lib/schema";
import { site } from "../../lib/site";

const updatedDate = new Date("2026-08-02");
const updated = new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-IE", {
  year: "numeric",
  month: "long",
  day: "numeric",
}).format(updatedDate);
const isoUpdated = updatedDate.toISOString().split("T")[0];

const pageUrl = new URL("/privacy/", site.url).toString();
const pageTitle = "Privacy · Dylan Collins";
const pageDesc =
  "What happens to the details you send through this site, who processes them, and how to have them deleted.";
---

<Base title={pageTitle} description={pageDesc}>
  <Schema
    slot="head"
    data={[
      webPageSchema({ url: pageUrl, name: pageTitle, description: pageDesc }),
      breadcrumbSchema([
        { name: "Home", url: site.url + "/" },
        { name: "Privacy", url: pageUrl },
      ]),
    ]}
  />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 lg:px-10 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <header class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-10 mb-16 lg:mb-24">
      <div class="hidden lg:block lg:col-span-2 section-num lift">Legal / Privacy</div>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-10 flex flex-col gap-5">
        <h1 class="display text-[clamp(2.75rem,7vw,4.5rem)] lift lift-1">
          Privacy<span class="text-accent">.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-ink-dim max-w-2xl lift lift-2">
          The short version: the only thing this site collects is what you type
          into a form, I use it to reply to you, and you can have it deleted by
          asking. The longer version is below.
        </p>
        <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint lift lift-3">
          Last updated · <time datetime={isoUpdated}>{updated}</time>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-10" data-reveal>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-2 section-num">Who</div>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-10 prose">
        <p>
          This site is run by {site.business.legalName}, trading as
          {site.business.tradingName}. {site.business.structure}. For anything on
          this page, the contact is
          <a href={`mailto:${site.author.email}`}>{site.author.email}</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          I am the data controller for the details you send me here, which under
          the GDPR means the decisions about what happens to them are mine, and
          so is the responsibility.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rule my-12 lg:my-16"></div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-10" data-reveal>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-2 section-num">What</div>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-10 prose">
        <p>Two forms on this site collect personal data, and nothing else does.</p>
        <p>
          <strong>The contact form</strong> takes your name, your email address
          and your message.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>The project brief</strong> takes the same, plus your business
          name, your website, which service you are asking about, your budget
          band, your timeline, and how you found me. Everything after the name,
          email and description is optional in practice: leave anything blank
          that you would rather not share, and I will ask if I genuinely need it.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is no analytics on this site, no advertising, no tracking pixels
          and no cookies set by me. I do not know who visits, only that someone
          did.
        </p>
        <p>
          One exception worth naming: a couple of the concept pages under
          <code>/demos/</code> load fonts from Google Fonts, which means your
          browser makes a request to Google when you open them. No other page
          does this.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rule my-12 lg:my-16"></div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-10" data-reveal>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-2 section-num">Why</div>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-10 prose">
        <p>
          To reply to you. That is the whole purpose. Where you are asking about
          hiring me, the lawful basis is that the processing is necessary to take
          steps at your request before entering a contract. For a general message
          it is my legitimate interest in answering people who write to me.
        </p>
        <p>
          I do not add you to a mailing list, I do not run a follow-up sequence,
          and I do not sell, rent or share your details with anyone for marketing.
          If you never reply to me, you will not hear from me again.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rule my-12 lg:my-16"></div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-10" data-reveal>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-2 section-num">Where</div>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-10 prose">
        <p>
          A form submission passes through three services before it reaches me,
          and each one is a processor acting on my instructions.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the site and runs the small
            function that receives the form. It sees your submission in transit
            and your IP address, which it uses to block abuse and rate limit the
            form. It does not store the submission.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Resend</strong> turns the submission into the two emails: the
            notification to me, and the confirmation to you. It holds a copy of
            those emails as part of delivering them.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>My email provider</strong> holds the message from the point
            it lands in my inbox.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Some of these providers process data outside the European Economic
          Area, principally in the United States. Where they do, the transfer
          relies on the safeguards in their own data processing terms, such as
          the European Commission's standard contractual clauses.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rule my-12 lg:my-16"></div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-10" data-reveal>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-2 section-num">How long</div>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-10 prose">
        <p>
          Enquiries that do not turn into work are deleted within two years, and
          usually a lot sooner. If we do end up working together, the records
          that go with that become business records, and Irish tax law requires
          me to keep those for six years.
        </p>
        <p>Ask me to delete something sooner and I will, unless the law says otherwise.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rule my-12 lg:my-16"></div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-10" data-reveal>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-2 section-num">Your rights</div>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-10 prose">
        <p>
          Under the GDPR you can ask me for a copy of what I hold about you, ask
          me to correct it, ask me to delete it, ask me to restrict what I do
          with it, object to my processing it, or ask for it in a portable
          format. Email
          <a href={`mailto:${site.author.email}`}>{site.author.email}</a> and I
          will come back to you within a month. There is no charge.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are not happy with how I handle it, you can complain to the
          Irish Data Protection Commission at
          <a href="https://www.dataprotection.ie" target="_blank" rel="noopener">dataprotection.ie</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rule my-12 lg:my-16"></div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-10" data-reveal>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-2 section-num">Changes</div>
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-10 prose">
        <p>
          If what this site does with your data changes, this page changes on the
          same day, and the date at the top moves with it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
